CORE
JmlOld
--function JmlOld.increment --jml-source src/main/java/JmlOld.java --unwind 5 -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
--
Regression for JML \old() in postconditions.

Verifies that the JML pipeline correctly:
- Parses \old(expr) into a history_exprt(expr, ID_old)
- Captures the pre-state value at function entry into a fresh
  symbol __jml_old_<idx>, declared and assigned via DECL/ASSIGN
- Substitutes history_exprt occurrences in ensures with the
  fresh symbol so symex can evaluate the postcondition

The increment() method takes a parameter x and returns x+1; the
JML postcondition compares \result to \old(x) + 1, which holds.
